## Why This Is Asked
This probes practical Azure Policy usage, Private Endpoints, tagging discipline, and CI/CD gating with rollback in a beginner-friendly way.

## Key Concepts
- Azure Policy deny public network access for storage accounts
- Private Endpoints and private DNS configuration
- Resource tagging as policy gates in CI/CD
- Rollback to last known-good ARM/Bicep template
- Monitoring and alerting via Azure Monitor

## Code Example
```json
{
  "properties": {
    "displayName": "Deny public network access on storage accounts",
    "policyType": "Regular",
    "mode": "All",
    "policyRule": {
      "if": {
        "allOf": [
          {"field": "type", "equals": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts"},
          {"field": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts/networkAcls/defaultAction", "equals": "Allow"}
        ]
      },
      "then": {"effect": "Deny"}
    }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt this for multi-region storage and cross-tenant sharing?
- How would you test the CI gate to minimize false positives and ensure rollback works?

## Why This Is Asked
Demonstrates practical understanding of basic Azure security controls: private networking, secret management, and policy enforcement in a real-world setup.

## Key Concepts
- Private Endpoints and Storage Account network rules
- Azure Policy to deny public access on storage and require private endpoints
- Key Vault references for secrets in App Settings
- Lightweight rollback and validation in CI/CD

## Code Example
```json
{
  "policyRule": {
    "if": { "field": "type", "equals": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts" },
    "then": { "effect": "deny" }
  }
}
```

```json
{
  "connectionStrings": {
    "DefaultConnection": "@Microsoft.KeyVault(SecretUri=https://kv-demo.vault.azure.net/secrets/DbConn/abc)"
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test rollback if private endpoints fail to provision?
- What are the trade-offs of denying public access vs. private endpoints in a multi-region setup?
